# Auth tokens for the two providers. This file is gitignored (copied to .env.secrets).
# main.ts reads .env.secrets directly — sandcastle's resolveEnv does NOT read it,
# so each token stays isolated to the sandbox that needs it. NEVER put these in
# .env (would leak to every sandbox → 401). See docs/adr/0001-sandcastle-cross-provider-split.md.
#
# Which keys you need depends on the active profile (SANDCASTLE_PROFILE, `split` by
# default): only the tokens of the providers that profile references are required,
# and main.ts checks them at startup. See docs/adr/0002-sandcastle-model-profiles.md.
#
#   profile `split` (default) — needs BOTH keys below
#     planner / implementer / merger → z.ai        reviewer → Anthropic native
#   profile `opus`             — needs CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN only
#     all four roles              → Anthropic native
#
# Run `SANDCASTLE_DRYRUN=1 npm run sandcastle` (or `npm run sandcastle:opus`) to
# print the active profile and which tokens it needs, without launching an agent.

# z.ai (GLM 5.2) — required by profile `split`
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Anthropic native (Claude Opus 5) — required by both profiles
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
